translated_text:
NUMBER 2 OF 2016

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN

AND CHILD VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF BATU BARA,

Considering:
a. b.
c. d. that every citizen has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of Violence;

that Women and Children are among vulnerable groups who tend to experience Violence which constitutes an act that violates human rights and need to receive legal Protection;

that the implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence needs to be supported by institutions and regulations so that its implementation can be guaranteed;

that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence;

In View of:

1. * Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
3. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic \ of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
4. Law Number 5 of 2007 concerning the Establishment of Batu Bara Regency in the Province of North Sumatra (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 7, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4681);
5. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
6. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
8. Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
9. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
10. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;

: \

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 2036);
18. Regional Regulation of Batu Bara Regency Number 1 of 2009 concerning Government Affairs that are the Authority of the Government of Batu Bara Regency;

With Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BATU BARA REGENCY and

text:
Pasal 2

Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan, dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas:
a. penghormatan dan pemenuhan terhadap hak-hak Korban;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi;
d. kepentingan terbaik bagi korban; dane. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2

Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of the rights of Victims;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. best interests of victims; ande. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 3

Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan bertujuan: a. mencegah segala bentuk kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. melindungi perempuan dan memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; danc. pemberdayaan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 3

Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to: a. prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. protect women and provide services to women and children victims of violence; andc. empower women and children victims of violence.

text:
HAK-HAK KORBAN

Pasal 4

Setiap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan berhak: a. untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia; b. untuk mendapatkan perlindungan dari keluarga, masyarakat, Pemerintah Daerah dan/ atau pihak lain baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan perintah perlindungan dari pengadilan;
c. atas pemulihan kesehatan fisik, psikologis maupun seksual sesuai penderitaan yang dialami korban kekerasan;
t.: l H .  d. atas penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban;
e. atas pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial dan bantuan hukum pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
f. atas pelayanan bimbingan rohani; dang. menentukan sendiri keputusannya.

translated_text:
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 4

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right: a. to have their dignity respected as a human being; b. to receive protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
c. to recovery of physical, psychological and sexual health according to the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
t.: l H .  d. to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; andg. to determine their own decisions.

text:
BAB IV

KEWAJIBAN DAN TANGGUNG JAWAB

Pasal 5

1. Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
2. Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan berdasarkan peraturan perundang undangan;
b. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
c. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
d. mengalokasikan anggaran dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
e. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 5

1. The Regional Government is obligated and responsible for providing protection to women and children victims of violence.
2. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children victims of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence;
d. allocating budget in the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 6

1. Masyarakat berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
2. Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diselenggarakan dalam bentuk:a. mencegah teijadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. memberikan perlindungan terhadap korban;
c. memberikan pertolongan darurat;
d. memberikan informasi dan/atau melaporkan tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak kepada. pihak yang berwenang; dane. turut serta dalam penanganan korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 6

1. The community is obligated and responsible for providing protection to women and children victims of violence.
2. The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out in the form of:a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing protection to victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to the competent authorities; ande. participating in the handling of victims of violence.

text:
BAB V

KELEMBAGAAN

:Pasal 7 (1) Dalam menyelenggarakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan di Daerah, Bupati dapat membentuk PPT.

2. Pembentukan dan pengembangan PPT disesuaikan dengan perkembangan prioritas kebutuhan, dan kemampuan keuangan Daerah serta kemampuan kelembagaan dan personil yang ada di Daerah.
3. PPT sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat mewadahi lembaga/unit keija yang memberikan pelayanan bagi korban kekerasan seperti P2TP2A, Rumah Aman, Rumah Perlindungan Sosial Anak, Rumah Perlindungan Trauma Center, Rumah Perlindungan Sosial Wanita, Rumah Singgah dan lain-lain kegiatan pelayanan sesuai peraturan perundang-undangan yang berlaku.
4. Bentuk pelayanan yang dilaksanakan PPT, meliputi:a. pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. bantuan hukum;
e. pemulangan; dan !f. reintegrasi sosial.
5. Dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan PPT berkewajiban:a. memberikan layanan secepat mungkin dan tanpa biaya kepada Korban;
b. menyelenggarakan Perlindungan dan pemenuhan hak korban atas Rehabilitasi Kesehatan, Rehabilitasi Sosial, Pemulangan, reintegrasi sosial dan bantuan hukum;
c. melakukan keijasama dengan lembaga tertentu dalam penyediaan penteijemah dan relawan pendamping j^ang diperlukan bagi Korban;

di' melakukan jejaring dengan rumah sakit pemerintah atau swasta untuk perawatan dan pemulihan kesehatan Korban serta melakukan kerjasama dengan lembaga Perlindungan saksi dan Korban, rumah Perlindungan sosial atau pusat trauma milik pemerintah, masyarakat, atau lembaga lembaga lainnya untuk pemulihan kesehatan korban;

:
e. memberikan kemudahan, kenyamanan, dan keselamatan bagi korban;
f. menjaga kerahasiaan korban;
g. memberikan pemenuhan bantuan hukum bagi korban; h. dalam hal penyelenggaraan pelayanan terpadu dilakukan secara berjejaring, PPT tetap bertanggung jawab atas keseluruhan proses rujukan pelayanan yang diperlukan korban.
6. Pemberian layanan terpadu sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) dilaksanakan sesuai dengan SPM.

translated_text:
CHAPTER V

INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS

:Article 7 (1) In providing protection for women and children victims of violence in the Region, the Regent may establish an IPU.

2. The establishment and development of IPU shall be adjusted to the development of priority needs, and the financial capacity of the Region as well as the institutional and personnel capacity available in the Region.
3. The IPU as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Child Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Protection Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
4. The forms of services implemented by the IPU include:a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal aid;
e. repatriation; and !f. social reintegration.
5. In providing protection for women and children victims of violence, the IPU is obligated to:a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to Victims;
b. organize Protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to Health Rehabilitation, Social Rehabilitation, Repatriation, social reintegration and legal aid;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants required for Victims;

d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of Victims and cooperate with the Witness and Victim Protection Agency, social Protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for the health recovery of victims;

:
e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for victims;
f. maintain the confidentiality of victims;
g. provide fulfillment of legal aid for victims; h. in the event that integrated service delivery is carried out through networking, the IPU remains responsible for the entire referral process of services required by victims.
6. The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented in accordance with MSS.

